| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[baritenor]] ([[Scientific pitch notation|A{{flat}}<sub>2</sub>]]–C<sub>5</sub>, [[falsetto]] to G<sub>5</sub>)
| Title role, leader of the [[Twelve Disciples|twelve disciples]], called the "Son of God" and the "King of the Jews".
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Judas Iscariot]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[tenor]] (B<sub>2</sub>–D<sub>5</sub>, falsetto E<sub>5</sub>)
| One of Jesus' twelve apostles; concerned for the poor and the consequences of Jesus's fame.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|{{nowrap|[[Mary Magdalene]]}}
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|{{nowrap|[[mezzo-soprano]] (F<sub>3</sub>–E{{flat}}<sub>5</sub>)}}
| A follower of Jesus who finds herself falling in love with him.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Pontius Pilate]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;" |[[baritenor]] (A<sub>2</sub>–B{{flat}}<sub>4</sub>)
| Roman Governor of Judea who foresees the events of Jesus's crucifixion from beginning to aftermath in a dream and finds himself being presented with that very situation.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Caiaphas]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Bass (voice type)|bass]]-[[baritone]] (C{{sharp}}<sub>2</sub>–F<sub>4</sub>)
| High priest and leader of the Pharisees who sees Jesus as a threat to the nation.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Annas]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[countertenor]] (G<sub>3</sub>–D<sub>5</sub>)
| Fellow priest at the side of Caiaphas who is persuaded by Caiaphas into seeing Jesus as a threat.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Saint Peter|Peter]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[baritone]] (A<sub>2</sub>–G<sub>4</sub>)
| One of Jesus's twelve apostles; denies Jesus three times upon the night of Jesus's arrest to save himself.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Simon the Zealot|Simon Zealotes]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[tenor]] (G<sub>3</sub>–B<sub>4</sub>)
| One of Jesus's twelve apostles; urges Jesus to lead his followers into battle against the Romans.
|- valign="top"
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[Herod Antipas|King Herod]]
| style="text-align: left; vertical-align:middle;"|[[baritone]] (B<sub>2</sub>–G<sub>4</sub>)
| The King of Galilee; Jesus is brought to him for judgment after first being taken to Pilate.
|}

== Musical numbers ==
{{col-begin}}
{{col-2}}
'''Act One'''
* "Overture" – Orchestra
* "Heaven on Their Minds" – [[Judas Iscariot|Judas]]
* "What's the Buzz/Strange Thing, Mystifying" – [[Jesus Christ|Jesus]], Judas, [[Mary Magdalene|Mary]] and [[Twelve Apostles|Apostles]]
* "[[Everything's Alright (Jesus Christ Superstar song)|Everything's Alright]]" – Mary, Judas, Jesus, Women and Apostles
* "[[This Jesus Must Die]]" – [[Caiaphas]], [[Annas]], and [[High Priest of Israel#In Christianity|High Priests]]
* "Hosanna" – Jesus, Caiaphas and Company
* "Simon Zealotes/Poor Jerusalem" – [[Simon Zealotes|Simon]], Jesus and Company
* "Pilate's Dream" – [[Pontius Pilate|Pilate]]
* "The Temple" – Jesus and Ensemble
* "Everything's Alright (Reprise)" – Mary and Jesus
* "[[I Don't Know How to Love Him]]" – Mary
* "Damned for All Time/Blood Money" – Judas, Caiaphas, Annas, and Ensemble
{{col-2}}
'''Act Two'''
* "The Last Supper" – Jesus, Judas, and Apostles
* "Gethsemane (I Only Want to Say)" – Jesus
* "The Arrest" – Judas, Jesus, [[Saint Peter|Peter]], Apostles, Caiaphas, Annas, and Ensemble
* "Peter's Denial" – Maid by the Fire, Peter, Soldier, Old Man, and Mary
* "Pilate and Christ" – Pilate, Jesus, Soldier, and Ensemble
* "King Herod's Song" – [[Herod Antipas|Herod]]
* "Could We Start Again Please?" – Mary, Peter, Apostles, and Women
* "Judas' Death" – Judas, Caiaphas, Annas, and Ensemble
* "Trial Before Pilate" – Pilate, Caiaphas, Jesus, and Ensemble
* "[[Superstar (Jesus Christ Superstar song)|Superstar]]" – Judas, Soul Sisters, and Angels
* "The Crucifixion" – Jesus and Ensemble
* "John Nineteen: Forty-One" – Orchestra
{{col-end}}

